      "question": "How do I identify my exact motherboard model without opening the computer case?",
      "answer": "Press Win + R, type msinfo32, and press Enter to launch System Information. Under System Summary, locate BaseBoard Manufacturer, BaseBoard Product, and BaseBoard Version. Alternatively, run Get-CimInstance -ClassName Win32_BaseBoard in PowerShell to retrieve the exact manufacturer string and model number."
