      "question": "How can I remove blank rows without deleting or modifying my original raw data?",
      "answer": "Use Excel 365 dynamic array formulas. On a clean worksheet, enter =FILTER(A2:D100, BYROW(A2:D100, LAMBDA(r, COUNTA(r)>0))) or simpler =FILTER(A2:D100, A2:A100<>\"\"). This dynamically extracts only populated records into a separate destination range while keeping your original source workbook intact."
